group: C4v
formula: Cr(CO)6
construction: its two chemical groups
headline: 
source: MO levels: RHF, def2-SVP · 
note: Model: order and approximate spacing from extended Hückel (qualitative) · calculation in eV · electrons: C5CrO5 56, drawn 56; CO 10, drawn 10; model and calculation: 66 drawn + 0 folded (0 levels) = 66 · labels in C<sub>4v</sub> (lowered from O<sub>h</sub> by the pick)\n10 high empty levels drawn at the top (not to scale); 17 levels have an overlap below 0.80 with the matched calculated orbital
about: The extended Hückel diagram explains the calculation's orbitals: nothing more, nothing less.\n\n**The model.** Every column is extended Hückel (Alvarez parameters). The middle column is the molecule's own extended Hückel run, the side columns are the two fragments' (C5CrO5 and CO). The basis is the same in all three, so the lines are an exact projection of each model MO on the fragment orbitals: a line joins a model MO to a fragment level that makes up at least 10 % of it.\n\n**Bonding and antibonding** are read from the sign of each model MO's overlap population between the two fragments: above +0.02 bonding, below -0.02 antibonding (*), otherwise non-bonding. A bonding and an antibonding level of the same degeneracy that are the in-phase and out-of-phase combinations of the same fragment orbitals are joined as partners and share a colour; a level without such a partner keeps its own classification.\n\n**Scale.** The model columns show the order of the levels and their approximate spacing from extended Hückel, not a scale: close levels are drawn further apart so they can be read, and no model energy is printed (it is in the hover text). Extended Hückel antibonding energies are qualitative and typically far too high for short bonds to diffuse atoms such as B, Be and Al.\n\n**The calculation** is the column on the right, on its own energy axis in eV (not on the model's scale). For each model level it shows the calculated orbital (or set of near-degenerate orbitals) with the largest overlap with it, at its calculated energy, in the colour of the model level it matches. Beside each matched level, "overlap" is |<model MO|calculated MO>| (a number from 0 to 1); values below 0.80 are counted in the note under the diagram. Labels are those of the matched calculated orbital. Clicking a level shows that orbital in 3-D.\n\nThe order of some empty levels above the LUMO differs between the model and the calculation. Virtual orbitals above the LUMO depend strongly on the basis set.\n\n**Total electrons: 66** (C5CrO5 56, CO 10).\n\nEach model level carries a short grey tag naming the fragment orbitals it is mostly made of (shares of at least 20 %), such as Cr d or CO π*. Ligand-field view hides empty ligand-centred levels such as CO π*; transitions into them are charge transfer, not d–d.\n\n**Caveats.** 10 high empty levels drawn at the top (not to scale); 17 levels have an overlap below 0.80 with the matched calculated orbital. Extended Hückel puts empty antibonding orbitals tens of eV up, so an empty level more than 30 eV above the HOMO is drawn at the top of the diagram, marked with an up arrow, or not at all when it sits almost entirely on one fragment. A loose match means no calculated orbital resembles the model level closely; read its calculated energy with care.\n\nDrawn as the two pieces left when the picked bond is cut, C5CrO5 and CO.\n\n**Orbital labels.** Symmetry labels computed from the orbitals in C4v; every level is the subduction of its label in the parent group, which the code's own labels validated.\n\nCutting Cr1–C2 does not keep the symmetry of the molecule (Oh); the orbitals are labelled in C4v, the largest subgroup that keeps the two sides.\n\n**Picked atoms.** One atom is drawn against the atoms bonded to it; two bonded atoms cut that bond and the two sides are drawn against each other (in and out of phase when they are equal). A metal gives the fragment-orbital diagram, each ligand being a connected piece left when the metal is removed.
verdict: differs The model puts 8e below 18a1, the model puts 7e below 18a1, the model puts 9e below 18a1; the calculation has those the other way round (5 of 91 pairs of the 14 levels judged). The empty levels differ: the calculated LUMO is 22a1, the model's is 14e.
